# Transcription Module

## WhisperKit

- Model: `base` (loaded async at startup)
- Input: 16 kHz Float32 mono audio
- Polling loop: every 2 seconds, drain samples from `AudioSource`
- Rolling buffer: capped at 30 seconds (`maxBufferSeconds`)
- Word timestamps enabled, clip timestamps used to avoid re-processing confirmed segments
- **Apple Silicon only** — WhisperKit requires the Neural Engine; on Intel (x86_64) it is hidden from the UI and cannot be selected
- `TranscriptionProvider.isAppleSilicon` (compile-time `#if arch(arm64)`) gates availability
- `TranscriptionProvider.availableProviders` filters `.whisperLocal` out on Intel
- `TranscriptionProvider.defaultProvider` returns `.whisperLocal` on ARM, `.sonioxCloud` on Intel
- `AppDelegate.makeTranscriptionService()` also guards against a stale persisted value

## Confirmation Lag

Segments are only committed (written to disk) when their `end` timestamp is **>4 seconds behind** the buffer head. Newer segments are treated as a live hypothesis — displayed but not persisted until confirmed.

## Transcript Format

- File: `~/Documents/NeverDrop/yyyy-MM-dd_HH-mm-ss.txt`
- Line format: `[MM:SS] transcribed text`
- The transcript directory path must come from a **single shared constant** (not duplicated)

## Error Handling

- Model load failure **must surface to the user** (status bar update or notification) — never silently leave `isModelLoaded = false`
- If transcription fails mid-session, log the error and notify the coordinator

## Future: Speaker Labels

When diarization is available, the transcript format should extend to `[MM:SS] [Speaker] text`. Design the `TranscriptWriter` interface to accept an optional speaker label now.
